# Trusted upstream proxies (CIDR notation, one per line).
# Used by rule 9522065 (@ipMatchFromFile) to decide whether to honour
# X-Forwarded-For. Enabled by default; the empty list trusts no peers.
#
# List the immediate REMOTE_ADDR peers that overwrite client-supplied XFF,
# including private addresses of internal load balancers or reverse proxies.
# Public provider ranges below are examples only when they are the immediate peer:
#
# Cloudflare:        https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v4 / https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v6
# AWS CloudFront:    https://d7uri8nf7uskq.cloudfront.net/tools/list-cloudfront-ips
# Google Cloud LB:   https://www.gstatic.com/ipranges/cloud.json
#
# Example (uncomment + replace with your values):
# 173.245.48.0/20
# 103.21.244.0/22
# 2400:cb00::/32
